    "title": "Drayton lays waste to fellow unbeaten team",
    "text": "DRAYTON — If Saturday’s regular-season finale between Drayton and fellow undefeated squad Center-Stanton was meant to be a preview of the upcoming 6-man football state championship game, the title game might not carry much suspense. But Drayton’s 59-0 victory wasn’t just about sending a message. This was, from the Bombers’ perspective, a celebration. Aside from injured starting quarterback Max Pokrzywinski, [[…]](https://www.wcrecord.com/articles/drayton-lays-waste-to-fellow-unbeaten-team/)\nYou must be a digital subscriber to access this content. Please login below or subscribe today!",
